#!/bin/sh
# A Saved Build (ADR 43 Q4, Q5; ADR 50 Q5): the release-type Enloq for
# arm64-v8a, built on the VPS from a clean committed HEAD at low priority, then
# handed to the running service, which keeps one Saved Build message in the
# Owner Account's own Saved Messages: it replaces that message's file and
# caption in place, and pins a newly posted one once. The caption names the
# version, commit, build time and the commits since the last one. The agent
# runs it after deploying a change to mobile/, shared/ or the API schema; the
# owner can run it at any time. Nothing is ever deleted from Saved Messages.
#
#   mobile/scripts/publish-android            build and post
#   mobile/scripts/publish-android --no-post  build and show the caption only
set -eu
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
root=$(cd .. && pwd)
post=yes
case "${1:-}" in
"") ;;
--no-post) post=no ;;
*)
  echo "usage: mobile/scripts/publish-android [--no-post]" >&2
  exit 2
  ;;
esac
if [ -n "$(git -C "$root" status --porcelain)" ]; then
  echo "Commit or stash first: Saved Builds come from committed revisions only." >&2
  exit 1
fi
umask 077
export LANG=en_US.UTF-8 LC_ALL=en_US.UTF-8 EXPO_NO_TELEMETRY=1 CI=1
. scripts/android-env
full=$(git -C "$root" rev-parse HEAD)
commit=$(git -C "$root" rev-parse --short=7 HEAD)
built=$(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)
version=$(node -p 'require("./app.json").expo.version')
name="enloq-$version-$commit.apk"
service="${ENLOQ_SERVICE_DIR:-$HOME/pi-workspace/enloq-service}"
# The last commit the service confirmed posting, kept in this checkout.
record="$root/.local/saved-build"
last=$(cat "$record" 2>/dev/null || true)

# The caption: at most ten commit subjects since the last Saved Build, with a
# count of the rest, within Telegram's 1,024 characters.
caption=$(ROOT="$root" LAST="$last" VERSION="$version" COMMIT="$commit" \
  BUILT="$built" python3 -I - <<'EOF'
import os
import subprocess

root, last = os.environ["ROOT"], os.environ["LAST"]
built = os.environ["BUILT"].replace("T", " ")[:16]


def git(*args):
    return subprocess.run(
        ["git", "-C", root, *args], capture_output=True, text=True
    )


lines = [f"Enloq {os.environ['VERSION']} · {os.environ['COMMIT']} · built {built} UTC"]
if last and git("merge-base", "--is-ancestor", last, "HEAD").returncode == 0:
    subjects = git("log", "--format=%s", f"{last}..HEAD").stdout.splitlines()
    if subjects:
        lines += ["", f"Since {last[:7]}:"]
        lines += [
            "• " + (s if len(s) <= 80 else s[:79] + "…") for s in subjects[:10]
        ]
        if len(subjects) > 10:
            lines.append(f"…and {len(subjects) - 10} more")
    else:
        lines += ["", "No commits since the last Saved Build."]
else:
    lines += ["", "The first Saved Build from this checkout."]
print("\n".join(lines)[:1024])
EOF
)

echo "Building $name…"
export ENLOQ_BUILD_COMMIT="$commit" ENLOQ_BUILD_TIME="$built"
# Native code for the S25's processor only (ADR 43 Q6).
export ORG_GRADLE_PROJECT_reactNativeArchitectures=arm64-v8a
npx expo prebuild --platform android --no-install >/dev/null
(cd android && $low ./gradlew --quiet app:assembleRelease)
apk=android/app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk
if [ ! -f "$apk" ]; then
  echo "The build made no APK." >&2
  exit 1
fi
if [ "$post" = no ]; then
  echo "Built $apk ($(du -h "$apk" | cut -f1)) and posted nothing. Its caption:"
  printf '%s\n' "$caption"
  exit 0
fi

# The service posts from its own data folder and deletes its copy once
# Telegram confirms; a failed post keeps it there, leaves the previous build
# in place and records nothing.
mkdir -p "$service/data/builds"
cp "$apk" "$service/data/builds/$name"
if printf '%s' "$caption" | docker exec -i "${ENLOQ_CONTAINER:-enloq}" \
  python -m enloq.saved --file "$name"; then
  mkdir -p "$root/.local"
  printf '%s\n' "$full" >"$record"
  echo "$name is in the Owner Account's Saved Messages."
else
  echo "The service did not post $name, so nothing was recorded." >&2
  exit 1
fi
